Design complete. **FC-4a passes all four contract metrics** — verdict `achieved`, audit chain closed (14 log entries, all evaluate verdicts mechanical via `bda log-evaluate`, `verify-deliverables: ALL PASS`).

## Final design — FC-4a (NMC811/graphite, Chen2020 base)

| Metric | Criterion | FC-4a | Source |
|---|---|---|---|
| Energy density | ≥ 327.18 Wh/kg | **427.04** ✓ (+30.5%) | `r3_fc4a_energy.json:energy_density_wh_kg` |
| 4C fast charge, no Li plating | anode ≥ 0 V | **+28.5 mV** ✓ (DFN, T_max 49.5 °C) | `r3_fc4a_4c_dfn.json:anode_potential_v` |
| SEI after 100 cyc @ 45 °C | ≤ 550 nm | **496.9 nm** ✓ | `r3_fc4a_aging45.json:sei_thickness_nm_end` |
| Nail 10 W, no thermal runaway | no trigger | **✓** T_max 36.1 °C (298 K start) / 49.5 °C (post-4C hot start) | `r3_fc4a_nail.json/_hot.json:triggered=false` |

**Design levers** (all five freedoms exercised): high-transport electrolyte σ 1.6 S/m / t⁺ 0.45 / D 3.0e-10 (literature-basis estimate, marked), negative particles 3.5→2.5 µm, negative porosity 0.34 / separator 0.58 / 9 µm, cooling h 10→170 W/m²K (hA 0.90 W/K).

**Key findings along the funnel:**
- **Baseline** failed two of four (ED 400.75 ✓, SEI 476 ✓, plating ✗ −0.19 V DFN, nail ✗ triggered 174.6 s)
- **Round 2** split the levers and failed both ways: transport-only (FC-1) passed 4C at +12.6 mV but lost the nail; cooling-only (FC-2) won the nail but cooled the cell to 324 K, where Arrhenius transport collapse re-introduced plating (−26 mV). The cooling↔fast-charge conflict is temperature-mediated — plating margin must be earned at the cooled operating temperature.
- **SPMe vs DFN divergence at 4C** (SPMe −0.43 V vs DFN +0.013 V for FC-1): per protocol, DFN is authoritative at high rate; round-1/2 4C verdicts were re-judged with DFN.
- Nail margin: hA 0.90 → steady state 309–323 K, >70 K below side-reaction onset (~385–400 K).

**Honest annotations in the record:** electrolyte parameters are estimates (real_compute=false; Stage 5 endorse recorded as skipped, no fabricated DFT/MD); aging capacity climb-saturate artifact labeled; the initial q=0 nail invocation was detected (`params.q_nail_W=0.0`) and rerun with q=10 W — reported values are the corrected runs; post-trigger T_max overshoot noted as numerical artifact, trigger judgment mechanical.

**Deliverables** (`runs/exp/t7_r1_flash/deliverables/`): `design_spec.md/pdf` (DS-001), `datasheet.md/pdf` (DSH-001), `dvpr.md/pdf` (DVPR-001), `dfmea.md/pdf` (DFMEA-001), `bom.xlsx/pdf` (BOM-001), `calc.xlsx/pdf` (CALC-001), `delivery_index.md/pdf` — all values mechanically sourced, per-line annotations, N/P ≈ 1.0 reported with cell-window caliber (the raw concentration caliber was found inconsistent with cell behavior and rejected with explanation). Plus `report.html` rendered from the log.
</text>
